{
  "title": "53: al-Najm النجم",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَالنَّجْمِ اِذَا هَوٰىۙ‏(1)\nWAALNNAJME EZAA HAWAA.\nBy the Star when it goes down, \nمَا ضَلَّ صَاحِبُكُمْ وَمَا غَوٰى‌ۚ‏(2)\nMAA ZALLA SAAHEBOKUM WA MAA GHAWAA.\nYour Companion is neither astray nor being misled. \nوَمَا يَنْطِقُ عَنِ الْهَوٰىؕ‏(3)\nWA MAA YANTEQU A’NIL AL-HAWAA.\nNor does he say (aught) of (his own) Desire. \nاِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا وَحْىٌ يُّوْحٰىۙ‏(4)\nIN HOWA ILLAA WAHAAUN YYOOHAA.\nIt is no less than inspiration sent down to him: \nعَلَّمَهٗ شَدِيْدُ الْقُوٰىۙ‏(5)\nA’ALLAMAH SHADEEDUL AL-QOOAA.\nHe was taught by one Mighty in Power, \nذُوْ مِرَّةٍؕ فَاسْتَوٰىۙ‏(6)\nZOO MERRATIN FAS-TAWAA.\nEndued with Wisdom: for he appeared (in stately form); \nوَهُوَ بِالْاُفُقِ الْاَعْلٰى ؕ‏(7)\nWA HOWA BIL-OFOQIL A-A’LAA.\nWhile he was in the highest part of the horizon: \nثُمَّ دَنَا فَتَدَلّٰىۙ‏(8)\nSUMMA DANAA FATADALLAA.\nThen he approached and came closer, \nفَكَانَ قَابَ قَوْسَيْنِ اَوْ اَدْنٰى‌ۚ‏(9)\nFA KAANA QAABA QAWSAYNE AW ADNAA.\nAnd was at a distance of but two bow-lengths or (even) nearer; \nفَاَوْحٰۤى الٰى عَبْدِهٖ مَاۤ اَوْحٰىؕ‏(10)\nFAAWHAA ALAA A’ABDEH MAA AAWHAA.\nSo did (Allah) convey the inspiration to His Servant- (conveyed) what He (meant) to convey. \nمَا كَذَبَ الْفُؤَادُ مَا رَاٰى‏(11)\nMAA KAZABA AL-FUAADU MAA RAAAA.\nThe (Prophet's) (mind and) heart in no way falsified that which he saw. \nاَفَتُمٰرُوْنَهٗ عَلٰى مَا يَرٰى‏(12)\nAAFATUMAAROONAH A’LAA MAA YARAA.\nWill ye then dispute with him concerning what he saw? \nوَلَقَدْ رَاٰهُ نَزْلَةً اُخْرٰىۙ‏(13)\nWA LAQAD RA-AAHO NAZLATAN LAHU.\nFor indeed he saw him at a second descent, \nعِنْدَ سِدْرَةِ الْمُنْتَهٰى‏(14)\nI’NDAL SEDRATE AL-MUNTAHAA.\nNear the Lote-tree beyond which none may pass: \nعِنْدَهَا جَنَّةُ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(15)\nE’ENDAHAA JANNATU AL-MAAWAA.\nNear it is the Garden of Abode. \nاِذْ يَغْشَى السِّدْرَةَ مَا يَغْشٰىۙ‏(16)\nIZ YAGHSHAN AS-SEDRATA MAA YAGHSHAA.\nBehold, the Lote-tree was shrouded (in mystery unspeakable!) \nمَا زَاغَ الْبَصَرُ وَمَا طَغٰى‏(17)\nMAA ZAAGHA BASARO WA MAA TAGHAA.\n(His) sight never swerved, nor did it go wrong! \nلَقَدْ رَاٰى مِنْ اٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِ الْكُبْرٰى‏(18)\nLAQAD RAAAA MIN AAYAATIL RABBEHIL KUBRAA.\nFor truly did he see, of the Signs of his Lord, the Greatest! \nاَفَرَءَيْتُمُ اللّٰتَ وَالْعُزّٰىۙ‏(19)\nAFARA-AYTOMUL AL-LAATA WAL U’UZZAA.\nHave ye seen Lat. and 'Uzza, \nوَمَنٰوةَ الثَّالِثَةَ الْاُخْرٰى‏(20)\nWAMANAAWTA AS-SAALESATA AL-AUKHRAA.\nAnd another, the third (goddess), Manat? \nاَلَكُمُ الذَّكَرُ وَلَهُ الْاُنْثٰى‏(21)\nAALAKUMU AZ-ZAKARU LAHUL AL-AUNSAA.\nWhat! for you the male sex, and for Him, the female? \nتِلْكَ اِذًا قِسْمَةٌ ضِيْزٰى‏(22)\nTILKA EZAL QESMATUN ZEEZAA.\nBehold, such would be indeed a division most unfair! \nاِنْ هِىَ اِلَّاۤ اَسْمَآءٌ سَمَّيْتُمُوْهَاۤ اَنْتُمْ وَاٰبَآؤُكُمْ مَّاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ بِهَا مِنْ سُلْطٰنٍ‌ؕ اِنْ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ وَمَا تَهْوَى الْاَنْفُسُ‌ۚ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَهُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمُ الْهُدٰىؕ‏(23)\nIN HEYA ILLAA AASMAAUN SAMMAYTUMOOHAA ANTUM WAABAAUKUM MAA ANZALAL LAAHO BEHAA MIN SULTAANIN IN YYATTABEU’OONA ILLAA AZ-ZANNA WA MAA TAHWAA AL-AANFUSU WA LAQAD JAAA-AHUM MIN RRABBEHEMU HODAA WA.\nThese are nothing but names which ye have devised, ye and your fathers, for which Allah has sent down no authority (whatever). They follow nothing but conjecture and what their own souls desire!- Even though there has already come to them Guidance from their Lord! \nاَمْ لِلْاِنْسَانِ مَا تَمَنّٰى   ۖ‏(24)\nAM INSAANIK MAA TAMANNAA.\nNay, shall man have (just) anything he hankers after? \nفَلِلّٰهِ الْاٰخِرَةُ وَالْاُوْلٰى‏(25)\nFALILLAAHE AAKHERATO WAL OOLAA.\nBut it is to Allah that the End and the Beginning (of all things) belong. \nوَكَمْ مِّنْ مَّلَكٍ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ لَا تُغْنِىْ شَفَاعَتُهُمْ شَيْئًا اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اَنْ يَّاْذَنَ اللّٰهُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَرْضٰى‏(26)\nWA MIN MMALAKIN FIL SAMAAWAATE LAA TUGHNEAA SHAFAAA’ATUHUM SHAY-ANW ILLAA MIN BA’DE AN YYAAZANA LAAHO LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YARZAA.\nHow many-so-ever be the angels in the heavens, their intercession will avail nothing except after Allah has given leave for whom He pleases and that he is acceptable to Him. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ لَيُسَمُّوْنَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ تَسْمِيَةَ الْاُنْثٰى‏(27)\nINNAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE LAYUSAMMOONA AL-MALAAAEKATA TASMEETA AL-AUNSAA.\nThose who believe not in the Hereafter, name the angels with female names. \nوَمَا لَهُمْ بِهٖ مِنْ عِلْمٍ‌ؕ اِنْ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ‌ۚ وَاِنَّ الظَّنَّ لَا يُغْنِىْ مِنَ الْحَقِّ شَيْئًاۚ‏(28)\nWA MAA LAHUM BEHI MIN E’ELMIN IN YYATTABEU’OONA ILLAA AZ-ZANNA WA INNA AZ-ZANNA LAA YUGHNEE MENAL HAQQE SHAY-ANW.\nBut they have no knowledge therein. They follow nothing but conjecture; and conjecture avails nothing against Truth. \nفَاَعْرِضْ عَنْ مَّنْ تَوَلّٰى ۙ عَنْ ذِكْرِنَا وَلَمْ يُرِدْ اِلَّا الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا ؕ‏(29)\nFAAA’REZ A’N MAN TAWALLAA A’N ZEKRENAA WA LAM YURED ILLAA HAYAATAD DUNYAA.\nTherefore shun those who turn away from Our Message and desire nothing but the life of this world. \nذٰ لِكَ مَبْلَغُهُمْ مِّنَ الْعِلْمِ‌ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ ضَلَّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ ۙ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنِ اهْتَدٰى‏(30)\nZAA LEKA MABLAGHUHUM MENAL I’LME INNAL RABBAKA HOWA A-A’LAMO BEMAN ZALLA A’N SABEELEH WA HOWA A-A’LAMO BE-MANIS TADAA.\nThat is as far as knowledge will reach them. Verily thy Lord knoweth best those who stray from His Path, and He knoweth best those who receive guidance. \nوَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِۙ لِيَجْزِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اَسَآءُوْا بِمَا عَمِلُوْا وَيَجْزِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اَحْسَنُوْا بِالْحُسْنٰى‌ ۚ‏(31)\nLILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE LE-YAJZEYAL LAZEENA AASAAOOA BEMAA A’MELOO WAYAJZEAAA LAZEENA AAHSANOOA BIL-HUSNAA.\nYea, to Allah belongs all that is in the heavens and on earth: so that He rewards those who do evil, according to their deeds, and He rewards those who do good, with what is best. \nاَلَّذِيْنَ يَجْتَنِبُوْنَ كَبٰٓئِرَ الْاِثْمِ وَالْفوَاحِشَ اِلَّا اللَّمَمَ‌ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ وَاسِعُ الْمَغْفِرَةِ‌ؕ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِكُمْ اِذْ اَنْشَاَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ وَاِذْ اَنْتُمْ اَجِنَّةٌ فِىْ بُطُوْنِ اُمَّهٰتِكُمْ‌ۚ فَلَا تُزَكُّوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْ‌ ؕ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنِ اتَّقٰى‏(32)\nLAZEENA YAJTANEBOONA KABAAAERA AL-AESME WAL FWAAHESHA ILLAA AL-LAMAMA INNAL RABBAKA WAASEU’U AL-MAGHFERATE HOWA A-A’LAMO BEKUM IZ AN-SHA-A MENAL ARZE WA IZ ANTUM AAJENNATUN FEE BUTOONE MINHUNNA FALAA TUZAKKOOA ANFOSAKUM HOWA A-A’LAMO BE-MANIS WAA.\nThose who avoid great sins and shameful deeds, only (falling into) small faults, verily thy Lord is ample in forgiveness. He knows you well when He brings you out of the earth, And when ye are hidden in your mothers' wombs. Therefore justify not yourselves: He knows best who it is that guards against evil. \nاَفَرَءَيْتَ الَّذِىْ تَوَلّٰىۙ‏(33)\nAAFARAAYTA LAZEE TAWALLAA.\nSeest thou one who turns back, \nوَاَعْطٰى قَلِيْلًا وَّاَكْدٰى‏(34)\nWA A-A’TAA QALEELAA WWAAKDAA.\nGives a little, then hardens (his heart)? \nاَعِنْدَهٗ عِلْمُ الْغَيْبِ فَهُوَ يَرٰى‏(35)\nAAE’ENDAH I’LMUS GHAYBE FAHOWA YARAA.\nWhat! Has he knowledge of the Unseen so that he can see? \nاَمْ لَمْ يُنَبَّاْ بِمَا فِىْ صُحُفِ مُوْسٰىۙ‏(36)\nAM LAM YUNABBAA BEMAA FEE SOHOFE MOOSAA.\nNay, is he not acquainted with what is in the Books of Moses- \nوَاِبْرٰهِيْمَ الَّذِىْ وَفّٰىٓ  ۙ‏(37)\nWA IBRAAHEEMA LAZEE WAFFAA.\nAnd of Abraham who fulfilled his engagements? \nاَلَّا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِّزْرَ اُخْرٰىۙ‏(38)\nALLAA TAZERU WAAZERATUN WWEZRA LAHU.\nNamely, that no bearer of burdens can bear the burden of another; \nوَاَنْ لَّيْسَ لِلْاِنْسَانِ اِلَّا مَا سَعٰىۙ‏(39)\nWA LLAYSA INSAANIK ILLAA MAA SA-A’A.\nThat man can have nothing but what he strives for; \nوَاَنَّ سَعْيَهٗ سَوْفَ يُرٰى‏(40)\nWA ANNAL SAA’YAH SAWFA YURAA.\nThat (the fruit of) his striving will soon come in sight: \nثُمَّ يُجْزٰٮهُ الْجَزَآءَ الْاَوْفٰىۙ‏(41)\nSUMMA YUJZAAHU AL-JAZAAA AL-AAWFAA.\nThen will he be rewarded with a reward complete; \nوَاَنَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ الْمُنْتَهٰىۙ‏(42)\nWA ANNAL ELAA RABBEKA AL-MUNTAHAA.\nThat to thy Lord is the final Goal; \nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ اَضْحَكَ وَاَبْكٰىۙ‏(43)\nWA ANNAHU HOWA AAZHAKA WAABKAA.\nThat it is He Who granteth Laughter and Tears; \nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ اَمَاتَ وَ اَحْيَا ۙ‏(44)\nWA ANNAHU HOWA AAMAATA WA AAHYAA.\nThat it is He Who granteth Death and Life; \nوَاَنَّهٗ خَلَقَ الزَّوْجَيْنِ الذَّكَرَ وَالْاُنْثٰىۙ‏(45)\nWA ANNAHU KHALAQAL AZ-ZAWJAYNE KHALAQAZ WAL AUNSAA.\nThat He did create in pairs, male and female, \nمِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ اِذَا تُمْنٰى‏(46)\nMIN NUTFATIN EZAA TUMNAA.\nFrom a seed when lodged (in its place); \nوَاَنَّ عَلَيْهِ النَّشْاَةَ الْاُخْرٰىۙ‏(47)\nWA ANNAL A’LAYHE NASH-ATAL AL-AUKHRAA.\nThat He hath promised a Second Creation (Raising of the Dead); \nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ اَغْنٰى وَ اَقْنٰىۙ‏(48)\nWA ANNAHU HOWA AGHNAA WA AAQNAA.\nThat it is He Who giveth wealth and satisfaction; \nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ رَبُّ الشِّعْرٰىۙ‏(49)\nWA ANNAHU HOWA RABBUL ASH-SHEA’RAA.\nThat He is the Lord of Sirius (the Mighty Star); \nوَاَنَّهٗۤ اَهْلَكَ عَادَا۟ اۨلْٮئُوْلٰى ۙ‏(50)\nWA ANNAHU AHLAKA A’AADAA AL-OOLAA.\nAnd that it is He Who destroyed the (powerful) ancient 'Ad (people), \nوَثَمُوْدَا۟ فَمَاۤ اَبْقٰىۙ‏(51)\nWASAMOODAA FAMAA AABQAA.\nAnd the Thamud nor gave them a lease of perpetual life. \nوَقَوْمَ نُوْحٍ مِّنْ قَبْلُ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا هُمْ اَظْلَمَ وَاَطْغٰىؕ‏(52)\nWA QAWMA NOOHIN MIN QABL WA INNAHUM KAANOO HUM AZLAMA WAATGHAA.\nAnd before them, the people of Noah, for that they were (all) most unjust and most insolent transgressors, \nوَالْمُؤْتَفِكَةَ اَهْوٰىۙ‏(53)\nWAL MUTAFEKATA AAHWAA.\nAnd He destroyed the Overthrown Cities (of Sodom and Gomorrah). \nفَغَشّٰٮهَا مَا غَشّٰى‌ۚ‏(54)\nFAGHASSHAAHAA MAA GHASSHAA.\nSo that (ruins unknown) have covered them up. \nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكَ تَتَمَارٰى‏(55)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKA TATAMAARAA.\nThen which of the gifts of thy Lord, (O man,) wilt thou dispute about? \nهٰذَا نَذِيْرٌ مِّنَ النُّذُرِ الْاُوْلٰٓى‏(56)\nHAAZAA NAZEERUM MENAL AN-NUZURE AL-AOOLAAA.\nThis is a Warner, of the (series of) Warners of old! \nاَزِفَتِ الْاٰزِفَةُ‌ۚ‏(57)\nAAZEFATE AL-AAAZEFATU.\nThe (Judgment) ever approaching draws nigh: \nلَيْسَ لَهَا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ كَاشِفَةٌ ؕ‏(58)\nLAYSA LAHAA MIN DOONIL LAAHE KAASHEFATUN.\nNo (soul) but Allah can lay it bare. \nاَفَمِنْ هٰذَا الْحَدِيْثِ تَعْجَبُوْنَۙ‏(59)\nAAFAMEN HAAZAA HAAZAL TAA’JABOONA.\nDo ye then wonder at this recital? \nوَتَضْحَكُوْنَ وَلَا تَبْكُوْنَۙ‏(60)\nWATAZHAKOONA WA LAA TABKOONA.\nAnd will ye laugh and not weep, \nوَاَنْتُمْ سٰمِدُوْنَ‏(61)\nWA ANTUM SAAMEDOONA.\nWasting your time in vanities? \nفَاسْجُدُوْا لِلّٰهِ وَاعْبُدُوْا ۩‏(62)\nFA JODOO LILLAAHE WA BODOO.\nBut fall ye down in prostration to Allah, and adore (Him)! [[۩]] ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Najm (The Star)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 26 verses. The reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of believers and sinners combined. The reciter will lead a respectable and honourable life and people will love and respect him.\nWriting this Surah and keeping it at a talisman makes one courageous in front of the ruler and makes the ruler respect him. He also comes out victorious in debates and discussions."
}
